  "question": {
    "text": "Three infinite plane sheets carrying uniform charge densities $-\\sigma, 2 \\sigma, 4 \\sigma$ are placed parallel to $X Z$ plane at $Y=a, 3 a$, 4a respectively. The electric field at the point $(0,2 a, 0)$ is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{5 \\sigma}{2 \\varepsilon_{0}} \\hat{j}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$-\\frac{7 \\sigma}{2 \\varepsilon_{0}} \\hat{j}$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{\\sigma}{2 \\varepsilon_{0}} \\hat{j}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{5 \\sigma}{-2 \\varepsilon_{0}} \\hat{\\mathrm{j}}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"assets\\st0015_4332218a2c85.png\"><br>\r\n$\\begin{aligned} \\mathrm{E}_{\\text {net }} &=7 \\mathrm{E} \\\\ &=7 \\frac{\\sigma}{2 \\varepsilon_{0}} \\text { alone }-\\text { ve } \\mathrm{Y} \\text {-axis } \\\\ & \\therefore \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{E}}=-\\frac{7 \\sigma}{2 \\varepsilon_{0}} \\hat{\\mathrm{j}} \\end{aligned}$"
